From 8d27914d3bcab6c2b10a9b07fd5200301af7bb5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:03:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: take a HEVC stream as its decoder gives it where
 its VUI says PQ or HLG

FFmpeg leaves the colour of the container in the parameters of a stream,
while its HEVC decoder gives every picture the colour description of the
VUI of the stream's sequence parameter set. A Matroska or MP4 file that
says BT.2020-10 (or BT.709, or no transfer) for a stream whose VUI says
HLG was HLG on the display, from its pictures, but SDR for everything
decided before its first picture: its HDR type, the change of mode held
for its HDR signalling, HLG sent as Dolby Vision, the whole-number
multiples of its frame rate, the library. The same for a VUI of PQ under
another transfer, and for a VUI of HLG under PQ.

PROGRESSIVE_VIDEO::HevcVuiColour() reads the colour description with the
parse of the sequence parameter set that the progressive check already
has, as FFmpeg 9.0.2 sets it (reserved and unnamed values unspecified),
from an hvcC record or Annex B, and only where every SPS of the base layer
has one and they agree. CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::TakeDecoderColour() takes it for
the stream where its transfer is PQ or HLG and the container says
another, and says so in the log. A VUI of BT.2020-10 or BT.709 under a
container's HLG is not taken: that is how an HLG stream speaks to decoders
that do not know HLG, with an alternative transfer characteristics SEI in
its packets that says HLG (DVB's HLG10), so the container's HLG stays, and
the log says that too. Files whose container and VUI agree do not change.

Found by SamuriHL in his CoreELEC builds (a walker of the SPS of its own
there).

Tests (outside the tree): 14 Matroska files made with mkvmerge 97 from
HEVC streams whose VUI says HLG, PQ or BT.2020-10 (with and without an
alternative transfer characteristics SEI, two with Dolby Vision) under
containers that contradict or agree with it, opened as the demuxer opens
them with FFmpeg 9.0.2 and run through the real TakeDecoderColour() and
DetermineHdrType(): wherever the VUI says PQ or HLG the stream says what
the decoder gives its pictures, and the files that agree are unchanged;
before the change 16 checks fail. HevcVuiColour() against FFmpeg 9.0.2's
decoder on every HEVC stream of 27 files (10 VUI variants made with
hevc_metadata, Dolby Vision samples, a transport stream) and on 8 records
put together: 45 checks. 9 mutants, each seen.
